        {
          "abilityId": 6,
          "accessMode": "ro",
          "code": "phase_a",
          "description": "1. Phase A voltage, current, and power\n2. Big-endian, HEX, total 8 bytes\n3. Units/precision: voltage 2 bytes, 0.1V; current 3 bytes, 0.001A; Phase A active power 3 bytes, 0.0001kW\n4. Message format\nExample: 08 80 00 03 E8 00 27 10 means Phase A 217.6V, Phase A current 1.000A, Phase A power 10.000kW\n5. Communication logic:\n1) When user enters the panel, it actively queries. The panel immediately sends 0x08 to the meter; the meter reports data to the cloud; the panel receives and displays it. Note: supported by latest Wi-Fi.\n2) The meter reports periodically. Recommendation: Wi-Fi mode report every 15s; NB mode report every 1 hour.",
          "extensions": {
            "iconName": "icon-dp_lightning",
            "attribute": "1152"
          },
          "name": "Phase X Voltage, Current and Power",
          "typeSpec": {
            "type": "raw",
            "maxlen": 128
          }
        },
        {
          "abilityId": 7,
          "accessMode": "ro",
          "code": "phase_b",
          "description": "1. Phase B voltage, current, and power\n2. Big-endian, HEX, total 8 bytes\n3. Units/precision: voltage 2 bytes, 0.1V; current 3 bytes, 0.001A; Phase B active power 3 bytes, 0.0001kW\n4. Message format\nExample: 08 80 00 03 E8 00 27 10 means Phase B 217.6V, Phase B current 1.000A, Phase B power 10.000kW\n5. Communication logic:\n1) When user enters the panel, it actively queries. The panel immediately sends 0x00 to the meter; the meter reports data to the cloud; the panel receives and displays it.\n2) The meter reports periodically. Recommendation: Wi-Fi mode report every 15s; NB mode report every 1 hour.",
          "extensions": {
            "iconName": "icon-dp_lightning",
            "attribute": "1152"
          },
          "name": "Phase Y Voltage, Current and Power",
          "typeSpec": {
            "type": "raw",
            "maxlen": 128
          }
        },
        {
          "abilityId": 8,
          "accessMode": "ro",
          "code": "phase_c",
          "description": "1. Phase C voltage, current, and power\n2. Big-endian, HEX, total 8 bytes\n3. Units/precision: voltage 2 bytes, 0.1V; current 3 bytes, 0.001A; Phase C active power 3 bytes, 0.0001kW\n4. Message format\nExample: 08 80 00 03 E8 00 27 10 means Phase C 217.6V, Phase C current 1.000A, Phase C power 10.000kW\n5. Communication logic:\n1) When user enters the panel, it actively queries. The panel immediately sends 0x08 to the meter; the meter reports data to the cloud; the panel receives and displays it.\n2) The meter reports periodically. Recommendation: Wi-Fi mode report every 15s; NB mode report every 1 hour.",
          "extensions": {
            "iconName": "icon-dp_lightning",
            "attribute": "1152"
          },
          "name": "Phase Z Voltage, Current and Power",
          "typeSpec": {
            "type": "raw",
            "maxlen": 128
          }
        },
        {
          "abilityId": 9,
          "accessMode": "ro",
          "code": "fault",
          "description": "1. Alarm\n2. Big-endian, HEX, 4 bytes\n3. Message format\nReport alarms as a full 4 bytes, mapping alarms to bits: 1 means alarm, 0 means no alarm. Unused alarm bits are padded with 0; undefined high bits are also padded with 0.\nExample: 0x00 00 00 09 indicates leakage self-test abnormal alarm and short-circuit alarm, with no other alarms.\n4. Communication logic\nAs long as any alarm occurs, report the full 4 bytes to the panel; as long as any alarm clears, report the full 4 bytes to update the panel display.",
          "extensions": {
            "iconName": "icon-baojing",
            "scope": "fault",
            "attribute": "1664"
          },
          "name": "Fault Alarm",
          "typeSpec": {
            "type": "bitmap",
            "label": [
              "short_circuit_alarm",
              "surge_alarm",
              "overload_alarm",
              "leakagecurr_alarm",
              "temp_dif_fault",
              "fire_alarm",
              "high_power_alarm",
              "self_test_alarm",
              "ov_cr",
              "unbalance_alarm",
              "ov_vol",
              "undervoltage_alarm",
              "miss_phase_alarm",
              "outage_alarm",
              "magnetism_alarm",
              "credit_alarm",
              "no_balance_alarm"
            ],
            "maxlen": 17
          }
        },
        {
          "abilityId": 12,
          "accessMode": "rw",
          "code": "clear_energy",
          "description": "",
          "extensions": {
            "iconName": "icon-dp_lightning",
            "attribute": "1024"
          },
